Data (data/manifest.json, data/scores.json, data/curate.json,
data/overrides.json): to the extent the curation, scores, and captions in
these files are protectable at all, they are dedicated to the public domain
under CC0 1.0 <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>. The
metadata they aggregate comes from CC0 sources (The Met, Art Institute of
Chicago, Cleveland Museum of Art, National Gallery of Art, Wikidata, and the
Rijksmuseum's CC0 API).

The artworks themselves are public domain or CC0; each work's licence
evidence is recorded per-work in the manifest, with a link to the holding
collection.
